== My church

#poem[][

My church has all the same people \
From when Gramma started bringing me \
They're just not all there anymore

My church has brass cleaned with a toothbrush \
Just the one lady who does this \
I don't have the heart to tell her that I \
Can't tell the difference \
Except that it's taking me thirtysome years \
To love God a fraction of how much she does \
In an afternoon \
While the light walks from one \
Stained glass story to the next \
In the nave, Jesus stands at the door and knocks \
Behind the rood screen, He teaches disciples

I sit in the gallery, away from all their eyes \
For staying so long \
But listening so little

